```

### Anti-Patterns to Avoid

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Fix |
|-------------|---------|-----|
| `"use client"` on a page that only displays data | Unnecessary client boundary | Remove directive, keep as Server Component |
| Direct API fetch in Client Component | Double-rendering, slower TTFB | Fetch in Server Component, pass as props |
| Dashboard page with inline data fetching in Client Component | Breaks server rendering pattern | Move fetch to Server Component |

## Route Handler Patterns

API routes (`src/app/api/**/route.ts`):

### Required Structure

```typescript
import { NextResponse } from "next/server";
import { z } from "zod";
import { logger } from "@/lib/logger";

const requestSchema = z.object({
  // define expected fields
});

export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const requestId = crypto.randomUUID();
  const log = logger.child({ requestId });

  try {
    log.info("api.request.start", { method: "POST", path: req.url });

    const body = await req.json();
    const parsed = requestSchema.safeParse(body);

    if (!parsed.success) {
      return NextResponse.json(
        { error: "Invalid request body", details: parsed.error.flatten() },
        { status: 400 }
      );
    }

    // ... business logic ...

    log.info("api.request.success", { /* outcome data */ });
    return NextResponse.json({ data: result }, { status: 200 });
  } catch (error) {
    log.error("api.request.error", { error: String(error) });
    return NextResponse.json(
      { error: "Internal server error" },
      { status: 500 }
    );
  }
}
```

### Response Shape Consistency

| Outcome | Shape | Status Code |
|---------|-------|-------------|
| Success | `{ data: ... }` | 200/201 |
| Validation Error | `{ error: "...", details?: ... }` | 400 |
| Unauthorized | `{ error: "Unauthorized" }` | 401 |
| Not Found | `{ error: "Resource not found" }` | 404 |
| Server Error | `{ error: "Internal server error" }` | 500 |

### Authentication in Route Handlers

```typescript
// GOOD — use auth() helper
import { auth } from "@/lib/auth";

export async function GET(req: Request) {
  const session = await auth();
  if (!session?.user) {
    return NextResponse.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 });
  }
  // ...
}

// BAD — read session from cookies manually
const cookies = req.headers.get("cookie");
```

## Onboarding Page Special Pattern

The onboarding page (`src/app/(auth)/onboarding/page.tsx`) is a Client Component because it requires:
- Chat streaming with SSE
- Real-time state updates
- OAuth popup handling
- localStorage persistence

This is an exception to the "default to Server Components" rule. It must remain a Client Component.

## Verification

Before committing changes:

- [ ] Dashboard pages are Server Components (no `"use client"`)
- [ ] API routes have proper error handling with logging
- [ ] API routes validate inputs with Zod
- [ ] Route handlers use `auth()` helper, not manual cookie parsing
- [ ] Response shapes are consistent (`{ data: ... }` or `{ error: ... }`)
- [ ] `pnpm run typecheck` passes (0 errors)
